{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@property","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"text":"nonatomic","kind":"keyword"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)NSExpression","text":"NSExpression","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" * ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hillshadeMethod","kind":"identifier"},{"text":";","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"languages":["occ"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default value of this property is an expression that evaluates to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"standard"},{"type":"text","text":". Set this property to "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to reset it to the default value."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can set this property to an expression containing any of the following:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Constant "},{"code":"MLNHillshadeMethod","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Any of the following constant string values:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"standard","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": The legacy hillshade method.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"basic"},{"text":": Basic hillshade. Uses a simple physics model where the reflected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"light intensity is proportional to the cosine of the angle between the incident","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"light and the surface normal. Similar to GDAL’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"gdaldem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" default algorithm.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"combined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": Hillshade algorithm whose intensity scales with slope. Similar","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to GDAL’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gdaldem"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"-combined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" option.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"igor"},{"text":": Hillshade algorithm which tries to minimize effects on other map","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"features beneath. Similar to GDAL’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"gdaldem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"-igor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" option.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"multidirectional","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": Hillshade with multiple illumination directions. Uses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the basic hillshade model with multiple independent light sources.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Predefined functions, including mathematical and string operators","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Conditional expressions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Variable assignments and references to assigned variables","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Step functions applied to the "},{"code":"$zoomLevel","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" variable"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This property does not support applying interpolation functions to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$zoomLevel"},{"type":"text","text":" variable or applying interpolation or step functions to feature"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attributes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The hillshade algorithm to use, one of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNHillshadeMethodStandard"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNHillshadeMethodBasic"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNHillshadeMethodCombined"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNHillshadeMethodIgor"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNHillshadeMethodMultidirectional"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"occ","url":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHillshadeStyleLayer\/hillshadeMethod"},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"hillshadeMethod","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"MapLibre"}],"title":"hillshadeMethod","role":"symbol","externalID":"c:objc(cs)MLNHillshadeStyleLayer(py)hillshadeMethod","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"hillshadeMethod","kind":"identifier"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHillshadeStyleLayer"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnhillshadestylelayer\/hillshademethod"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}]}],"references":{"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Powerful, free and open-source mapping toolkit with full control over data sources and styling."}],"title":"MapLibre","role":"collection"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNHillshadeStyleLayer/hillshadeMethod":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHillshadeStyleLayer\/hillshadeMethod","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnhillshadestylelayer\/hillshademethod","abstract":[{"text":"The hillshade algorithm to use, one of ","type":"text"},{"code":"MLNHillshadeMethodStandard","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"MLNHillshadeMethodBasic","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"MLNHillshadeMethodCombined","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNHillshadeMethodIgor"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNHillshadeMethodMultidirectional"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "}],"title":"hillshadeMethod","fragments":[{"text":"hillshadeMethod","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNHillshadeStyleLayer":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHillshadeStyleLayer","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnhillshadestylelayer","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHillshadeStyleLayer"},{"type":"text","text":" is a style layer that renders raster "},{"type":"text","text":"digital elevation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"model"},{"type":"text","text":" (DEM) tiles on the map."}],"title":"MLNHillshadeStyleLayer","fragments":[{"text":"MLNHillshadeStyleLayer","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"}}}